welcome back to las vegas now  recognizing the symptoms of an  overactive bladder can be life-changing  for many we checked in with the urology  specialist of nevada the sponsors of  this next segment for answers  so obviously a lot of women and men are  affected you know on their day-to-day  lives with bladder issues but let's  break it down a little bit let's talk  about an overactive bladder can you tell  us a little bit more about that and what  that really means of course so  overactive bladder um is also known as  urge urinary incontinence  it is the involuntary loss of urine  associated with a sudden urge to go  very common can affect up to 25 million  americans  75 to 80 of those are women mostly over  50.  um and very very common very treatable i  think a lot of people maybe feel  embarrassed to go to the doctor for this  and even once they're there to to bring  it up and be open about discussing it so  what are some tips or advice you have  for people who may be struggling with  this and want to get in and see a  specialist exactly so  i think understanding that they're not  alone not the only ones going through  this that it does interfere with quality  of life it can affect your ability to  work  sleep socialize travel perform daily  functions so knowing that again it is  very common it is very treatable and  let's talk about treatments what types  of treatments are available to those out  there who might be suffering from this  we we start from very conservative to  more invasive so first and foremost we  talk about behavioral modifications  timed urination  avoiding  lots of fluids in the evening hours we  talk about pelvic floor exercises so the  the  the pelvis sits on a muscular floor and  strengthening that pelvic floor can you  can suppress the urge to void i even get  physical therapists involved there are  physical therapists who have special  training in female pelvic disorders they  can teach you again number one where  those muscles are number two how to  strengthen and rehabilitate them we talk  about lifestyle modifications uh  avoiding things which might be  irritating to the bladder the big  culprits there being coffee sodas teas  etc  spicy foods and um  a nicotine big big big bladder irritant  so stop smoking etc and then we move on  to medications there's different types  of medications we use all which  help to improve the ability of the  bladder to store urine beyond  medications we do use botox in the  bladder so just like folks get botox  elsewhere to kind of decrease muscle  spasticity we can do botox in the  bladder to improve the ability of the  bladder to store urine and there are uh  there is nerve stimulation we do by  providing low level stimulation to  nerves that supply the bladder that too  so that's kind of getting a little bit  more advanced but again anywhere from  just some lifestyle changes to  medications to the to the more advanced  yeah as i tell my patients not always  can we cure incontinence but we can  definitely improve it  thank you again to the urology urology  specialist of nevada for sponsoring that  segment they have four locations across  southern nevada where they can help you  or your loved ones for more information  call 702  877-0814 or visit usonb.com  we'll be right back
 

